**Verdict:** `revise` — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. **1 blocker, 6 concerns.**

**Strongest hit (ENN-H1):** the marker read as an address — *"A marker is an address, and an address is a place you can be expected to return to and sit in. He would fill the grave with his own hands and then make certain there was nowhere to go back to."* It works because the load-bearing element is Wright's own sentence rather than an interpreted behavior, it ties directly to the Seven's core fear as 9takes states it, and it arrives after the man instead of instead of him. Runner-up is the Sullivan-residue paragraph, which names what the type *cannot* explain — rare enough in typology writing to be worth protecting on its own.

**Blocker (ENN-B1):** the diagnosis section's reframe paragraph says Wright "was in love again before the year was out," and the Mamah section says Noel "was living in the rebuilt house within months." The packet's December 1914 record is receipt and acknowledgment of a condolence letter; CLM-28 grades the cohabitation clause **unverified** with a competing account of 1916, and explicitly warns that this timeline is doing type-discriminating work against Type 4. The phrase "before the year was out" is graded nowhere in the claim inventory. Repair is two clause-level edits, net zero words — the Seven point survives, arguably harder.

**Highest-priority concern (ENN-C1):** Type 8 as core is never addressed, and it's the reading the draft's own showcase evidence invites — the cold open, a whole H2, the lead FAQ, the 60-ton column, firing his son over wages. The draft answers *which wing*, never *which core*. 9takes' own Harmonics page supplies the fix free: 7 is Positive Outlook (reframe, minimize), 8 is Reactive (feel it loud and make sure you feel it too). That separates delivery from operating system, which is exactly the confusion — "move your chair" is delivered as an Eight would deliver it and contains what only a Seven would say. One Rabbit Hole paragraph, ~70 words, no body change.

Two things worth your attention beyond the review: every repair I proposed is clause-level or word-negative because the draft sits at 4,488 against a 4,500 ceiling. And I flagged one out-of-lane error I didn't count — the three 1914 victims described as "apprentices," which packet D-07 marks *settled against* (draftsman, foreman, gardener). That belongs to the subject or critic reviewer, but it sits two paragraphs from the piece's best passage and shouldn't ride out on the assumption someone else caught it.
